  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Freeze-Out Dominoes (Children's Domino Game). Setup: Double-six dominoes, evenly distributed to 2-6 players; extras removed. Turn Sequence: Lead player reveals rightmost domino and announces its suits. Other players reveal their rightmost dominoes in turn. Trick Winner: Player whose domino matches one of the lead suits collects all revealed dominoes. Collected dominoes placed at left of line, face-down. Next Lead: Trick winner leads the next round. Game End: Last player remaining with dominoes wins. Win Condition: Accumulate all dominoes.",
    Player: 'Welcome to Freeze-Out Dominoes! You are playing a simple matching game. On your turn, reveal your rightmost domino. Try to match the suits from the lead tile to win the trick and collect all dominoes revealed. Be the first to gather all dominoes and you win!',
    objective: 'Be the first player to accumulate all dominoes by winning tricks.',
    gameplay: "1. **Lead Tile**: One player reveals the rightmost domino in their line and announces its two suits (or single suit if a double). 2. **Other Players' Turns**: Each other player, in turn, reveals their rightmost domino. 3. **Trick Winner**: The player whose revealed domino matches one of the two suits from the lead tile wins all face-up dominoes (the 'trick'). 4. **Captured Tiles**: The trick winner places captured dominoes at the left end of their line, face-down. 5. **Next Round**: The trick winner leads the next round by revealing their new rightmost domino. 6. **Elimination**: Players who run out of dominoes exit the game. 7. **Game End**: The last remaining player with dominoes wins.",
    keyRules: [
      'Dominoes must be arranged face-down in a single horizontal line.',
      'Players always reveal from the rightmost position in their line.',
      'To win a trick, a domino must match one (or both) suits of the lead tile.',
      'Captured dominoes are placed at the left of the line, face-down.',
      'The trick winner always leads the next round.',
      'Players eliminated when they have no dominoes left.',
      'Extras not distributed during dealing are removed from play entirely.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 to 6 players.',
      deck: 'Standard double-six domino set (28 tiles).',
      equipment: 'Dominoes, flat playing surface.',
      dealing: "Shuffle all dominoes face-down. Distribute evenly among players. If dominoes don't divide evenly, remove extras from play. Each player arranges their dominoes face-down in a horizontal line.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Lead Tile**: One player reveals the rightmost domino in their line and announces its two suits (or single suit if a double). 2. **Other Players' Turns**: Each other player, in turn, reveals their rightmost domino. 3. **Trick Winner**: The player whose revealed domino matches one of the two suits from the lead tile wins all face-up dominoes (the 'trick'). 4. **Captured Tiles**: The trick winner places captured dominoes at the left end of their line, face-down. 5. **Next Round**: The trick winner leads the next round by revealing their new rightmost domino. 6. **Elimination**: Players who run out of dominoes exit the game. 7. **Game End**: The last remaining player with dominoes wins.",
